concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-311 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "311 Simplified outline"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-311 ;
    values:originalText "The following is a simplified outline of this Part: • The ACMA, carriers and carriage service providers must prevent, so far as it is reasonably practicable to do so, telecommunications networks and facilities from being used to commit offences. • The ACMA, carriers and carriage service providers must give the authorities such help as is reasonably necessary for the purposes of:  (a) enforcing the criminal law and laws imposing pecuniary penalties; and  (b) protecting the public revenue; and  (c) safeguarding national security. • A carriage service provider may suspend the supply of a carriage service in an emergency if requested to do so by a senior police officer." ;
    skos:definition "The following is a simplified outline of this Part: • The ACMA, carriers and carriage service providers must prevent, so far as it is reasonably practicable to do so, telecommunications networks and facilities from being used to commit offences. • The ACMA, carriers and carriage service providers must give the authorities such help as is reasonably necessary for the purposes of:  (a) enforcing the criminal law and laws imposing pecuniary penalties; and  (b) protecting the public revenue; and  (c) safeguarding national security. • A carriage service provider may suspend the supply of a carriage service in an emergency if requested to do so by a senior police officer."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "637a88f8c161751da4dfbc126784b836b960139b47e91b64d70db6d70c1f3c6e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "29"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Must prevent use of telecommunications networks for committing offences." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.29" ;
