    skos:prefLabel "317B Definitions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-317b ;
    values:originalText "In this Part: access, when used in relation to material, includes:  (a) access that is subject to a pre-condition (for example, the use of a password); and  (b) access by way of push technology; and  (c) access by way of a standing request. ASIO affiliate has the same meaning as in the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979. ASIO employee has the same meaning as in the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979.   Industry assistance  Part 15 Introduction  Division 1  Section 317B  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  chief officer of an interception agency has the meaning given by section 317ZM. contracted service provider, in relation to a designated communications provider, means a person who performs services for or on behalf of the provider, but does not include a person who performs such services in the capacity of an employee of the provider. designated communications provider has the meaning given by section 317C. electronic protection includes:  (a) authentication; and  (b) encryption. electronic service has the meaning given by section 317D. eligible activities of a designated communications provider has the meaning given by section 317C. entrusted ASD person means a person who:  (a) is a staff member of the Australian Signals Directorate; or  (b) has entered into a contract, agreement or arrangement with the Australian Signals Directorate; or  (c) is an employee or agent of a person who has entered into a contract, agreement or arrangement with the Australian Signals Directorate. entrusted ASIO person means an entrusted person (within the meaning of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979). entrusted ASIS person means a person who:  (a) is a staff member or agent of the Australian Secret Intelligence Service; or  (b) has entered into a contract, agreement or arrangement with the Australian Secret Intelligence Service; or" ;
    skos:definition "In this Part: access, when used in relation to material, includes:  (a) access that is subject to a pre-condition (for example, the use of a password); and  (b) access by way of push technology; and  (c) access by way of a standing request. ASIO affiliate has the same meaning as in the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979. ASIO employee has the same meaning as in the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979.   Industry assistance  Part 15 Introduction  Division 1  Section 317B  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  chief officer of an interception agency has the meaning given by section 317ZM. contracted service provider, in relation to a designated communications provider, means a person who performs services for or on behalf of the provider, but does not include a person who performs such services in the capacity of an employee of the provider. designated communications provider has the meaning given by section 317C. electronic protection includes:  (a) authentication; and  (b) encryption. electronic service has the meaning given by section 317D. eligible activities of a designated communications provider has the meaning given by section 317C. entrusted ASD person means a person who:  (a) is a staff member of the Australian Signals Directorate; or  (b) has entered into a contract, agreement or arrangement with the Australian Signals Directorate; or  (c) is an employee or agent of a person who has entered into a contract, agreement or arrangement with the Australian Signals Directorate. entrusted ASIO person means an entrusted person (within the meaning of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979). entrusted ASIS person means a person who:  (a) is a staff member or agent of the Australian Secret Intelligence Service; or  (b) has entered into a contract, agreement or arrangement with the Australian Secret Intelligence Service; or"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a462771e322847d43c9894bc1570b4efa6c813e1c58b74a8dd8233cb4a3c68b9" ;
    cof:pageNumber "42"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines terms related to access, electronic protection, and designated communications providers." ;
