    cof:title "317ZQ(1) Delegation by Director-General of the Australian Signals" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Director-General of the Australian Signals Directorate may, by writing, delegate any or all of the functions or powers of the Director-General of the Australian Signals Directorate under Division 2 or 6 to a person:  (a) who is a staff member of the Australian Signals Directorate; and  (b) who:  (i) is an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the Australian Signals Directorate; or  (ii) holds, or is acting in, a position in the Australian Signals Directorate that is equivalent to, or higher than, a position occupied by an SES employee.   Industry assistance  Part 15 General provisions  Division 8  Section 317ZR  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "150"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-317zq-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "317ZQ(2) Delegation by Director-General of the Australian Signals"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-317zq-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A delegate must comply with any written directions of the Director-General of the Australian Signals Directorate." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A delegate must comply with any written directions of the Director-General of the Australian Signals Directorate."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "18b990145f2f49d51dbbf26da2e5c36edd6d9705c5bfc5f23c60f97f4106e439" ;
