concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-338-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "338(4) ACMA’s certification of draft agreement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-338-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) For the purposes of this section, in determining whether a particular matter is reasonable, the ACMA must have regard to:  (a) the needs of the Defence Department and of the Defence Force; and  (b) the interests of the carrier or carriage service provider concerned. This subsection does not, by implication, limit the meaning of the expression “reasonable”." ;
    skos:definition "(4) For the purposes of this section, in determining whether a particular matter is reasonable, the ACMA must have regard to:  (a) the needs of the Defence Department and of the Defence Force; and  (b) the interests of the carrier or carriage service provider concerned. This subsection does not, by implication, limit the meaning of the expression “reasonable”."@en ;
