concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-339 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "339 Requirement to enter into certified agreement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-339 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if the ACMA has certified a draft agreement relating to a carrier or carriage service provider.  (2) A defence authority may give:  (a) the carrier; or  (b) the carriage service provider; as the case requires, a written notice requiring the carrier or provider to enter into the agreement within 30 days after receiving the notice.  (3) The carrier or provider must comply with the notice." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if the ACMA has certified a draft agreement relating to a carrier or carriage service provider.  (2) A defence authority may give:  (a) the carrier; or  (b) the carriage service provider; as the case requires, a written notice requiring the carrier or provider to enter into the agreement within 30 days after receiving the notice.  (3) The carrier or provider must comply with the notice."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "21cbc135c154170eac28d496581355d3024ba93e3041118fe8ae0ab4a69c8d5e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "162"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-339-ss-1 ;
