concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-341 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "341 Withdrawal of certification of agreement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-341 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies if:  (a) a certified agreement is in force at a particular time; and  (b) the ACMA is of the opinion that, if the agreement were a draft agreement at that time, the ACMA would have refused to certify it.  (2) The ACMA must withdraw its certification of the agreement.   Defence requirements and disaster plans  Part 16 Defence planning  Division 3  Section 342  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (3) As soon as practicable after withdrawing its certification of the agreement, the ACMA must give each of the parties to the agreement a written notice stating that it has withdrawn its certification of the agreement." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies if:  (a) a certified agreement is in force at a particular time; and  (b) the ACMA is of the opinion that, if the agreement were a draft agreement at that time, the ACMA would have refused to certify it.  (2) The ACMA must withdraw its certification of the agreement.   Defence requirements and disaster plans  Part 16 Defence planning  Division 3  Section 342  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (3) As soon as practicable after withdrawing its certification of the agreement, the ACMA must give each of the parties to the agreement a written notice stating that it has withdrawn its certification of the agreement."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c0c620b69c7df11cbb3435f3e1c93589a72773e5a46560c07594565704526ce3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "162"^^xsd:integer ;
