doc:sec-349a-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "349A(2) Local access line" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purposes of this Part, a determination requires a carriage service provider (the first provider) to provide pre-selection in favour of another carriage service provider (the second provider) in relation to calls made using a particular carriage service if, and only if, the determination requires:  (a) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the first provider to permit an end-user to:  (i) pre-select the second provider as the end-user’s preferred carriage service provider for such of the end-user’s requirements, in relation to calls made using that carriage service, as are specified in the determination; and  (ii) change that selection from time to time; and  (c) the controlled networks and controlled facilities of the first provider to provide over-ride dial codes for selecting alternative carriage service providers, in relation to calls made using that carriage service, on a call-by-call basis. Note: End-user is defined by subsection (3)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "174"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-349a-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "349A(3) Local access line"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-349a-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) For the purposes of this section, an end-user, in relation to a controlled network or a controlled facility, is an end-user of a carriage service that involves the use of the network or facility." ;
    skos:definition "(3) For the purposes of this section, an end-user, in relation to a controlled network or a controlled facility, is an end-user of a carriage service that involves the use of the network or facility."@en ;
