concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "351 Pre-selection to be provided"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-351 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies to a person if a determination under section 349 is in force and that determination requires the person to provide pre-selection.  (2) A person must provide pre-selection in accordance with the requirements set out in the determination and on such terms and conditions as are:  (a) agreed between the following parties:  (i) the person;   Pre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17  Section 352  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (ii) the carriage service provider in whose favour pre-selection is required to be provided; or  (b) failing agreement, determined by an arbitrator appointed by the parties. If the parties fail to agree on the appointment of an arbitrator, the ACCC is to be the arbitrator.  (3) The regulations may make provision for and in relation to the conduct of an arbitration under this section.  (4) The regulations may provide that, for the purposes of a particular arbitration conducted by the ACCC under this section, the ACCC may be constituted by a single member, or a specified number of members, of the ACCC. For each such arbitration, that member or those members are to be nominated in writing by the Chairperson of the ACCC.  (5) Subsection (4) does not, by implication, limit subsection (3).  (6) A person must comply with any rules set out in the determination as mentioned in paragraph 349(1)(b) or (2)(b)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies to a person if a determination under section 349 is in force and that determination requires the person to provide pre-selection.  (2) A person must provide pre-selection in accordance with the requirements set out in the determination and on such terms and conditions as are:  (a) agreed between the following parties:  (i) the person;   Pre-selection in favour of carriage service providers  Part 17  Section 352  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (ii) the carriage service provider in whose favour pre-selection is required to be provided; or  (b) failing agreement, determined by an arbitrator appointed by the parties. If the parties fail to agree on the appointment of an arbitrator, the ACCC is to be the arbitrator.  (3) The regulations may make provision for and in relation to the conduct of an arbitration under this section.  (4) The regulations may provide that, for the purposes of a particular arbitration conducted by the ACCC under this section, the ACCC may be constituted by a single member, or a specified number of members, of the ACCC. For each such arbitration, that member or those members are to be nominated in writing by the Chairperson of the ACCC.  (5) Subsection (4) does not, by implication, limit subsection (3).  (6) A person must comply with any rules set out in the determination as mentioned in paragraph 349(1)(b) or (2)(b)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "72b4ff441b0a5da263bf89c330356d353f0425d82f837b263d27e20eb1f2015b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "176"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351-ss-4 ;
