concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "351(4) Pre-selection to be provided"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-351-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The regulations may provide that, for the purposes of a particular arbitration conducted by the ACCC under this section, the ACCC may be constituted by a single member, or a specified number of members, of the ACCC. For each such arbitration, that member or those members are to be nominated in writing by the Chairperson of the ACCC." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The regulations may provide that, for the purposes of a particular arbitration conducted by the ACCC under this section, the ACCC may be constituted by a single member, or a specified number of members, of the ACCC. For each such arbitration, that member or those members are to be nominated in writing by the Chairperson of the ACCC."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "64861dc687fc4a616622459cf0c465c75b45b3ee4e2eb27cbb156cd8fc5e3e45" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-351 ;
    cof:pageNumber "176"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The ACCC may be constituted by a single member or specified number of members for a particular arbitration." ;
    dc:description "Nominations in writing by the Chairperson of the ACCC" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
