concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-356 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "356 Exemptions from calling line identification requirement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-356 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA may, by notice in the Gazette, declare that a specified person is exempt from the requirement set out in section 355. The declaration has effect accordingly.   Calling line identification  Part 18  Section 356  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Note: A person may be identified by name, by inclusion in a particular class or in any other way.  (2) In deciding whether a person should be exempt from the requirement set out in section 355, the ACMA must have regard to the following matters:  (a) whether it would be unreasonable to impose the requirement;  (b) whether it is in the public interest to impose the requirement.  (3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which the ACMA may have regard." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACMA may, by notice in the Gazette, declare that a specified person is exempt from the requirement set out in section 355. The declaration has effect accordingly.   Calling line identification  Part 18  Section 356  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Note: A person may be identified by name, by inclusion in a particular class or in any other way.  (2) In deciding whether a person should be exempt from the requirement set out in section 355, the ACMA must have regard to the following matters:  (a) whether it would be unreasonable to impose the requirement;  (b) whether it is in the public interest to impose the requirement.  (3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which the ACMA may have regard."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "de05ac22a4e30dc8bef1cda5bb3db1daf427cad17a77e2680c2aad2afda96148" ;
    cof:pageNumber "180"^^xsd:integer ;
