doc:sec-356-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "356(1) Exemptions from calling line identification requirement" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA may, by notice in the Gazette, declare that a specified person is exempt from the requirement set out in section 355. The declaration has effect accordingly.   Calling line identification  Part 18  Section 356  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Note: A person may be identified by name, by inclusion in a particular class or in any other way." ;
    cof:pageNumber "180"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-356-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "356(2) Exemptions from calling line identification requirement"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-356-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) In deciding whether a person should be exempt from the requirement set out in section 355, the ACMA must have regard to the following matters:  (a) whether it would be unreasonable to impose the requirement;  (b) whether it is in the public interest to impose the requirement." ;
    skos:definition "(2) In deciding whether a person should be exempt from the requirement set out in section 355, the ACMA must have regard to the following matters:  (a) whether it would be unreasonable to impose the requirement;  (b) whether it is in the public interest to impose the requirement."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ffc522d707eee8f1b8ea5deacde9ce59e7fffa46389b0300f40b87e332478257" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-356 ;
    cof:pageNumber "180"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Consider exemptions from line identification requirement based on reasonableness and public interest." ;
