concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ab a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360AB Associate"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-360ab ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Part, an associate of a person (the first person) in relation to control of:  (a) a facility; or  (b) a company; is:  (c) a partner of the first person; or  (d) if the first person or another person who is an associate of the first person under another paragraph receives benefits or is capable of benefiting under a trust—the trustee of the trust; or  (e) a person (whether a company or not) who:  (i) acts, or is accustomed to act; or   Statutory infrastructure providers  Part 19 Introduction  Division 1  Section 360AC  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (ii) under a contract or an arrangement or understanding (whether formal or informal) is intended or expected to act;  in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of, or in concert with:  (iii) the first person; or  (iv) the first person and another person who is an associate of the first person under another paragraph; or  (f) another company if:  (i) the other company is a related body corporate of the first person for the purposes of the Corporations Act 2001; or  (ii) the first person, or the first person and another person who is an associate of the first person under another paragraph, is or are in a position to exercise control of the other company.  (2) However, persons are not associates of each other if the ACMA is satisfied that:  (a) they do not act together in any relevant dealings relating to the facility or company; and  (b) neither of them is in a position to exert influence over the business dealings of the other in relation to the facility or company." ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Part, an associate of a person (the first person) in relation to control of:  (a) a facility; or  (b) a company; is:  (c) a partner of the first person; or  (d) if the first person or another person who is an associate of the first person under another paragraph receives benefits or is capable of benefiting under a trust—the trustee of the trust; or  (e) a person (whether a company or not) who:  (i) acts, or is accustomed to act; or   Statutory infrastructure providers  Part 19 Introduction  Division 1  Section 360AC  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (ii) under a contract or an arrangement or understanding (whether formal or informal) is intended or expected to act;  in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of, or in concert with:  (iii) the first person; or  (iv) the first person and another person who is an associate of the first person under another paragraph; or  (f) another company if:  (i) the other company is a related body corporate of the first person for the purposes of the Corporations Act 2001; or  (ii) the first person, or the first person and another person who is an associate of the first person under another paragraph, is or are in a position to exercise control of the other company.  (2) However, persons are not associates of each other if the ACMA is satisfied that:  (a) they do not act together in any relevant dealings relating to the facility or company; and  (b) neither of them is in a position to exert influence over the business dealings of the other in relation to the facility or company."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cb2ac96733e4cede38088251fc2b811184dacb31f0c3ca4a42b8925f8e9d4f8f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "186"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ab-ss-1 ;
