doc:sec-360ha-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "360HA(1) Nominated service area—anticipatory notice to be given to" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) after the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) enters into a contract for the installation of telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in the whole or a part of the project area of a real estate development project; and  (b) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be required, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole or the part, as the case requires, of the project area is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes of this Part; the carrier must:  (c) give the ACMA a written notice that:  (i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and  (ia) sets out the date on which the contract was entered into; and  (ii) specifies the whole or the part, as the case requires, of the project area; and  (iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure that is to be installed under the contract; and   Statutory infrastructure providers  Part 19 Service areas and statutory infrastructure providers  Division 2  Section 360HA  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion date for the installation; and  (d) do so within 20 business days after entering into the contract. Note: For the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA." ;
    cof:pageNumber "198"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ha-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360HA(2) Nominated service area—anticipatory notice to be given to"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-360ha-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) If:  (a) before the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) entered into a contract for the installation of telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in the whole or a part of the project area of a real estate development project; and  (b) the installation was not completed before the commencement of this section; and  (c) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be required, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole or the part, as the case requires, of the project area is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes of this Part; the carrier must:  (d) give the ACMA a written notice that:  (i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and  (ii) specifies the whole or the part, as the case requires, of the project area; and  (iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure that is to be installed under the contract; and  (iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion date for the installation; and  (e) do so:  (i) within 90 days after the commencement of this section; or  (ii) if the ACMA allows a longer period—within that longer period. Note: For the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA." ;
    skos:definition "(2) If:  (a) before the commencement of this section, a carrier (other than an NBN corporation) entered into a contract for the installation of telecommunications network infrastructure that will enable the supply of eligible services to premises in the whole or a part of the project area of a real estate development project; and  (b) the installation was not completed before the commencement of this section; and  (c) when the installation is completed, the carrier will be required, by subsection 360H(2), to declare that the whole or the part, as the case requires, of the project area is a provisional nominated service area for the purposes of this Part; the carrier must:  (d) give the ACMA a written notice that:  (i) states that the carrier has entered into the contract; and  (ii) specifies the whole or the part, as the case requires, of the project area; and  (iii) describes the telecommunications network infrastructure that is to be installed under the contract; and  (iv) sets out the carrier’s estimate of the likely completion date for the installation; and  (e) do so:  (i) within 90 days after the commencement of this section; or  (ii) if the ACMA allows a longer period—within that longer period. Note: For the format of the description of the area, see section 360LA."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5d91055f79b1ef0a842f9b1f925d80454b58c384d6a632ee67ad67d41b39869b" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ha ;
    cof:pageNumber "198"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Carrier must give ACMA written notice within 90 days after commencement." ;
    dc:description "written notice stating contract details and estimated completion date" ;
