doc:sec-360ve-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "360VE(4) Time for payment of damages" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) If:  (a) a statutory infrastructure provider makes a decision under subsection (1) to accept a liability to pay damages to a particular customer; and  (b) the liability is to be discharged by giving the customer a credit in an account the customer has with the statutory infrastructure provider;   Statutory infrastructure providers  Part 19 Compensation  Division 4A  Section 360VF  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  the liability must be discharged within the period of 14 weeks after the decision is made and:  (c) if it is practicable for the statutory infrastructure provider to give the customer the credit within that 14-week period and in time for the customer to be notified of the credit in the first bill sent to the customer during that period—by giving the customer the credit in time for the customer to be notified of the credit in that bill; or  (d) if paragraph (c) does not apply, but it is practicable for the statutory infrastructure provider to give the customer the credit within that 14-week period and in time for the customer to be notified of the credit in the second bill sent to the customer during that period—by giving the customer the credit in time for the customer to be notified of the credit in that bill. Other manner of discharging liability" ;
    cof:pageNumber "248"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ve-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360VE(5) Time for payment of damages"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-360ve-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) If:  (a) a statutory infrastructure provider makes a decision under subsection (1) to accept a liability to pay damages to a particular customer; and  (b) the liability is not to be discharged by giving the customer a credit in an account the customer has with the statutory infrastructure provider; the liability must be discharged within 14 weeks after the decision is made. Customer" ;
    skos:definition "(5) If:  (a) a statutory infrastructure provider makes a decision under subsection (1) to accept a liability to pay damages to a particular customer; and  (b) the liability is not to be discharged by giving the customer a credit in an account the customer has with the statutory infrastructure provider; the liability must be discharged within 14 weeks after the decision is made. Customer"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c7e4e704db2a333d9b585e3bb876aa2393c6732abed6a719e5f6677cb725e010" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360ve ;
    cof:pageNumber "248"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Liability to pay damages must be discharged within 14 weeks after decision is made." ;
