concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360x a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360X Offer to be made available—supply of eligible services"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-360x ;
    values:originalText "(1) A statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must make available on its website:  (a) the terms and conditions relating to price or a method of ascertaining price; and  (b) other terms and conditions; on which it offers to supply eligible services to carriage service providers in order that the carriage service providers can provide   Statutory infrastructure providers  Part 19 Offers to be made available  Division 5  Section 360X  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  qualifying carriage services to end-users at premises in the service area.  (2) The terms and conditions mentioned in subsection (1) must include:  (a) the maximum period within which the statutory infrastructure provider must begin to supply such an eligible service following the making of a request by a carriage service provider; and  (b) the maximum period within which the statutory infrastructure provider must rectify a fault or service difficulty relating to such an eligible service following the making of a report by a carriage service provider about the fault or service difficulty.  (3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).  (4) An offer made available under subsection (1) has no effect to the extent to which it is inconsistent with:  (a) a standard determined under section 360U; or  (b) rules made under section 360V." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A statutory infrastructure provider for a service area must make available on its website:  (a) the terms and conditions relating to price or a method of ascertaining price; and  (b) other terms and conditions; on which it offers to supply eligible services to carriage service providers in order that the carriage service providers can provide   Statutory infrastructure providers  Part 19 Offers to be made available  Division 5  Section 360X  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  qualifying carriage services to end-users at premises in the service area.  (2) The terms and conditions mentioned in subsection (1) must include:  (a) the maximum period within which the statutory infrastructure provider must begin to supply such an eligible service following the making of a request by a carriage service provider; and  (b) the maximum period within which the statutory infrastructure provider must rectify a fault or service difficulty relating to such an eligible service following the making of a report by a carriage service provider about the fault or service difficulty.  (3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).  (4) An offer made available under subsection (1) has no effect to the extent to which it is inconsistent with:  (a) a standard determined under section 360U; or  (b) rules made under section 360V."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "783afdff9117d3433180d33875aedd5f190f4291f1f9ccb72f1724cc4ad60cda" ;
    cof:pageNumber "252"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360x-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360x-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360x-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360x-ss-4 ;
