concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360xa a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "360XA Periodic compliance reports"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-360xa ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules requiring each statutory infrastructure provider to give to the ACMA periodic reports relating to the provider’s compliance with this Part. Note: For variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Compliance  (2) A statutory infrastructure provider must comply with rules under subsection (1).  (3) A person is not excused from giving a report under rules under subsection (1) on the ground that the report might tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty.  (4) However, in the case of an individual:  (a) the report; or  (b) giving the report; or" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules requiring each statutory infrastructure provider to give to the ACMA periodic reports relating to the provider’s compliance with this Part. Note: For variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Compliance  (2) A statutory infrastructure provider must comply with rules under subsection (1).  (3) A person is not excused from giving a report under rules under subsection (1) on the ground that the report might tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty.  (4) However, in the case of an individual:  (a) the report; or  (b) giving the report; or"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "28c12d49be4c821a4cd34595da90584a8aeffc62da235c87e05ccda38856d8ca" ;
    cof:pageNumber "259"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360xa-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360xa-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360xa-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-360xa-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.259" .
doc:sec-360xa a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "360XA Periodic compliance reports" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules requiring each statutory infrastructure provider to give to the ACMA periodic reports relating to the provider’s compliance with this Part. Note: For variation and revocation, see subsection 33(3) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901. Compliance  (2) A statutory infrastructure provider must comply with rules under subsection (1).  (3) A person is not excused from giving a report under rules under subsection (1) on the ground that the report might tend to incriminate the person or expose the person to a penalty.  (4) However, in the case of an individual:  (a) the report; or  (b) giving the report; or" ;
    cof:pageNumber "259"^^xsd:integer .

