concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-366 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "366 Compliance with conventions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-366 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies to a person who is:  (a) a carrier; or   International aspects of activities of the telecommunications industry  Part 20 Compliance with international agreements  Division 2  Section 366  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) a carriage service provider.  (2) The Minister may, by notice published in the Gazette, declare that, for the purposes of this section, a specified convention is binding in relation to the members of a specified class of persons.  (3) A person who is a member of that class must, in connection with:  (a) the operation by the person of telecommunications networks or of facilities; or  (b) the supply by the person of carriage services; act in a way consistent with Australia’s obligations under that convention.  (4) The Minister may, by notice published in the Gazette, declare that, for the purposes of this section, a specified part of a specified convention is binding in relation to the members of a specified class of persons.  (5) A person who is a member of that class must, in connection with:  (a) the operation by the person of telecommunications networks or of facilities; or  (b) the supply by the person of carriage services; act in a way consistent with Australia’s obligations under that part of the convention.  (6) In this section: convention means:  (a) a convention to which Australia is a party; or  (b) an agreement or arrangement between Australia and a foreign country; and includes, for example, an agreement, arrangement or understanding between a Minister and an official or authority of a foreign country." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies to a person who is:  (a) a carrier; or   International aspects of activities of the telecommunications industry  Part 20 Compliance with international agreements  Division 2  Section 366  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) a carriage service provider.  (2) The Minister may, by notice published in the Gazette, declare that, for the purposes of this section, a specified convention is binding in relation to the members of a specified class of persons.  (3) A person who is a member of that class must, in connection with:  (a) the operation by the person of telecommunications networks or of facilities; or  (b) the supply by the person of carriage services; act in a way consistent with Australia’s obligations under that convention.  (4) The Minister may, by notice published in the Gazette, declare that, for the purposes of this section, a specified part of a specified convention is binding in relation to the members of a specified class of persons.  (5) A person who is a member of that class must, in connection with:  (a) the operation by the person of telecommunications networks or of facilities; or  (b) the supply by the person of carriage services; act in a way consistent with Australia’s obligations under that part of the convention.  (6) In this section: convention means:  (a) a convention to which Australia is a party; or  (b) an agreement or arrangement between Australia and a foreign country; and includes, for example, an agreement, arrangement or understanding between a Minister and an official or authority of a foreign country."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "edb5a80ae387e31ea924725f3be84748ff3b46a327e1739e76a808244a60e0c5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "266"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-366-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-366-ss-2 ;
