concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-369 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "369 Rules of Conduct to bind carriers and carriage service providers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-369 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies to a person who is:  (a) a carrier; or  (b) a carriage service provider.  (2) The person must comply with Rules of Conduct in force under section 367.  (3) If a provision of an agreement made by the person is inconsistent with Rules of Conduct in force under section 367, the provision is unenforceable (see section 370)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies to a person who is:  (a) a carrier; or  (b) a carriage service provider.  (2) The person must comply with Rules of Conduct in force under section 367.  (3) If a provision of an agreement made by the person is inconsistent with Rules of Conduct in force under section 367, the provision is unenforceable (see section 370)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "804841b1cd8b9c84ca32fb7eeab8d2e6dab2b5d7b32add151b7af23cd9154673" ;
    cof:pageNumber "271"^^xsd:integer ;
