doc:sec-372f a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "372F Installation of fibre-ready facilities—building units" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This section applies to the installation of a fixed-line facility in the project area, or any of the project areas, for a real estate development project if:  (a) the project involves the construction of one or more building units on one or more areas of land; and  (b) the installation occurs after the commencement of this section; and  (c) sewerage services, electricity or water is, are, or will be, supplied to those units." ;
    cof:pageNumber "281"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372g a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "372G Sale of building lots and building units—subdivisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-372g ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This section applies if:  (a) a real estate development project involves the subdivision of one or more areas of land into building lots; and  (b) the project involves either or both of the following:  (i) the making available of one or more of those lots for sale or lease, where it would be reasonable to expect that one or more building units would be subsequently constructed on the lots;  (ii) the construction of one or more building units on any of the lots and the making available of any of those building units for sale or lease; and  (c) if subparagraph (b)(i) applies—sewerage services, electricity or water is, are, or will be, supplied to those lots; and  (d) if subparagraph (b)(ii) applies—sewerage services, electricity or water is, are, or will be, supplied to those units. Note 1: For subdivision of an area of land, see section 372R. Note 2: For building lot, see section 372Q. Note 3: For building unit, see section 372S. Note 4: For sale of building lots, see section 372T. Note 5: For sale of building units, see section 372U. Note 6: For supply of sewerage services, electricity or water, see section 372Z. Note 7: For exemptions, see section 372K. Note 8: For exemption of certain projects, see section 372P." ;
    skos:definition "Scope  (1) This section applies if:  (a) a real estate development project involves the subdivision of one or more areas of land into building lots; and  (b) the project involves either or both of the following:  (i) the making available of one or more of those lots for sale or lease, where it would be reasonable to expect that one or more building units would be subsequently constructed on the lots;  (ii) the construction of one or more building units on any of the lots and the making available of any of those building units for sale or lease; and  (c) if subparagraph (b)(i) applies—sewerage services, electricity or water is, are, or will be, supplied to those lots; and  (d) if subparagraph (b)(ii) applies—sewerage services, electricity or water is, are, or will be, supplied to those units. Note 1: For subdivision of an area of land, see section 372R. Note 2: For building lot, see section 372Q. Note 3: For building unit, see section 372S. Note 4: For sale of building lots, see section 372T. Note 5: For sale of building units, see section 372U. Note 6: For supply of sewerage services, electricity or water, see section 372Z. Note 7: For exemptions, see section 372K. Note 8: For exemption of certain projects, see section 372P."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "adf638bb25414284c9150f5b8c61dd7959d4ea35ca713ea991de0a451ffb8403" ;
    cof:pageNumber "283"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Scope of subdivision of building lots and units" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.283" ;
