concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372ja a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "372JA Remedial notices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-372ja ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This section applies if the ACMA reasonably believes that a person:  (a) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or  (b) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in circumstances that make it likely that the contravention will continue or be repeated; or  (c) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty provision. Note: For designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH.   Deployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A Installation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3  Section 372JB  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Remedial notice  (2) The ACMA may give the person a written notice requiring the person to:  (a) remedy the contravention; or  (b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or  (c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or likely contravention.  (3) A notice under subsection (2) is to be known as a remedial notice." ;
    skos:definition "Scope  (1) This section applies if the ACMA reasonably believes that a person:  (a) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or  (b) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in circumstances that make it likely that the contravention will continue or be repeated; or  (c) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty provision. Note: For designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH.   Deployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A Installation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3  Section 372JB  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Remedial notice  (2) The ACMA may give the person a written notice requiring the person to:  (a) remedy the contravention; or  (b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or  (c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or likely contravention.  (3) A notice under subsection (2) is to be known as a remedial notice."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000" ;
    cof:pageNumber "288"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372ja-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372ja-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372ja-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.288" .
doc:sec-372ja a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "372JA Remedial notices" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This section applies if the ACMA reasonably believes that a person:  (a) is contravening a designated civil penalty provision; or  (b) has contravened a designated civil penalty provision in circumstances that make it likely that the contravention will continue or be repeated; or  (c) is likely to contravene a designated civil penalty provision. Note: For designated civil penalty provision, see section 372JH.   Deployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A Installation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3  Section 372JB  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  Remedial notice  (2) The ACMA may give the person a written notice requiring the person to:  (a) remedy the contravention; or  (b) prevent the likely contravention from occurring; or  (c) remedy the things or operations causing the contravention or likely contravention.  (3) A notice under subsection (2) is to be known as a remedial notice." ;
    cof:pageNumber "288"^^xsd:integer .

