doc:sec-372jc-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "372JC(3) Compliance with remedial notice" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Subsections (1) and (2) are civil penalty provisions. Note: Part 31 provides for pecuniary penalties for breaches of civil penalty provisions." ;
    cof:pageNumber "290"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372jd a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "372JD Extension of time for compliance with remedial notices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-372jd ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This section applies if a person has been given a remedial notice. Extension of compliance period  (2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the person, extend the compliance period for the remedial notice.  (3) However, the ACMA may extend the compliance period only if the period has not ended.   Deployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A Installation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3  Section 372JE  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (4) In this section, compliance period means the period stated in the remedial notice under section 372JB, and includes that period as extended under this section." ;
    skos:definition "Scope  (1) This section applies if a person has been given a remedial notice. Extension of compliance period  (2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the person, extend the compliance period for the remedial notice.  (3) However, the ACMA may extend the compliance period only if the period has not ended.   Deployment of optical fibre etc.  Part 20A Installation of fibre-ready facilities  Division 3  Section 372JE  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (4) In this section, compliance period means the period stated in the remedial notice under section 372JB, and includes that period as extended under this section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000" ;
