    skos:prefLabel "372JF(1) Revocation of remedial notices"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-372jf-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person has been given a remedial notice; and  (b) at a time during the compliance period for the notice, the ACMA forms a reasonable belief that the notice is no longer required for the purposes of requiring the person to:  (i) remedy a contravention of a designated civil penalty provision; or  (ii) prevent a likely contravention of a designated civil penalty provision from occurring; or  (iii) remedy the things or operations causing a contravention, or likely contravention, of a designated civil penalty provision; the ACMA must, by written notice given to the person, revoke the notice." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a person has been given a remedial notice; and  (b) at a time during the compliance period for the notice, the ACMA forms a reasonable belief that the notice is no longer required for the purposes of requiring the person to:  (i) remedy a contravention of a designated civil penalty provision; or  (ii) prevent a likely contravention of a designated civil penalty provision from occurring; or  (iii) remedy the things or operations causing a contravention, or likely contravention, of a designated civil penalty provision; the ACMA must, by written notice given to the person, revoke the notice."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d9d2f7a76e8e55a51cf7f425cad6a2c2e5e548074a47ab482ec8f14d56573429" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-372jf ;
