concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-386 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "386 Procedures for making technical standards"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-386 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Before making a technical standard under section 384, the ACMA must, so far as is practicable, try to ensure that:  (a) interested persons have had an adequate opportunity to make representations about the proposed standard (either directly, or indirectly by means of a report under paragraph (2)(g)); and  (b) due consideration has been given to any representations so made.  (2) The ACMA may make an arrangement with any of the following bodies or associations:  (a) Standards Australia;  (b) a body or association approved in writing by Standards Australia for the purposes of this subsection;  (c) a body or association specified in a written determination made by the ACMA for the purposes of this subsection; under which the body or association:  (d) prepares a draft of a standard; and  (e) publishes the draft standard; and  (f) undertakes a process of public consultation on the draft standard; and   Technical regulation  Part 21 Technical standards about the interconnection of facilities  Division 5  Section 387  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (g) reports to the ACMA on the results of that process of public consultation.  (3) A copy of an approval under paragraph (2)(b) is to be published in the Gazette.  (4) A copy of a determination under paragraph (2)(c) is to be published in the Gazette.  (5) For the purposes of subsection (1), interested persons are taken not to have had an adequate opportunity to make representations unless there was a period of at least 60 days during which the representations could be made." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Before making a technical standard under section 384, the ACMA must, so far as is practicable, try to ensure that:  (a) interested persons have had an adequate opportunity to make representations about the proposed standard (either directly, or indirectly by means of a report under paragraph (2)(g)); and  (b) due consideration has been given to any representations so made.  (2) The ACMA may make an arrangement with any of the following bodies or associations:  (a) Standards Australia;  (b) a body or association approved in writing by Standards Australia for the purposes of this subsection;  (c) a body or association specified in a written determination made by the ACMA for the purposes of this subsection; under which the body or association:  (d) prepares a draft of a standard; and  (e) publishes the draft standard; and  (f) undertakes a process of public consultation on the draft standard; and   Technical regulation  Part 21 Technical standards about the interconnection of facilities  Division 5  Section 387  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (g) reports to the ACMA on the results of that process of public consultation.  (3) A copy of an approval under paragraph (2)(b) is to be published in the Gazette.  (4) A copy of a determination under paragraph (2)(c) is to be published in the Gazette.  (5) For the purposes of subsection (1), interested persons are taken not to have had an adequate opportunity to make representations unless there was a period of at least 60 days during which the representations could be made."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cde7f0e77b74ac1c56c3e0cf21011970654508e3ccdbd83e225f1f2897c06efe" ;
    cof:pageNumber "322"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-386-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-386-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-386-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-386-ss-4 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-386-ss-5 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.322" .
doc:sec-386 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "386 Procedures for making technical standards" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Before making a technical standard under section 384, the ACMA must, so far as is practicable, try to ensure that:  (a) interested persons have had an adequate opportunity to make representations about the proposed standard (either directly, or indirectly by means of a report under paragraph (2)(g)); and  (b) due consideration has been given to any representations so made.  (2) The ACMA may make an arrangement with any of the following bodies or associations:  (a) Standards Australia;  (b) a body or association approved in writing by Standards Australia for the purposes of this subsection;  (c) a body or association specified in a written determination made by the ACMA for the purposes of this subsection; under which the body or association:  (d) prepares a draft of a standard; and  (e) publishes the draft standard; and  (f) undertakes a process of public consultation on the draft standard; and   Technical regulation  Part 21 Technical standards about the interconnection of facilities  Division 5  Section 387  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (g) reports to the ACMA on the results of that process of public consultation.  (3) A copy of an approval under paragraph (2)(b) is to be published in the Gazette.  (4) A copy of a determination under paragraph (2)(c) is to be published in the Gazette.  (5) For the purposes of subsection (1), interested persons are taken not to have had an adequate opportunity to make representations unless there was a period of at least 60 days during which the representations could be made." ;
    cof:pageNumber "322"^^xsd:integer .

