concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-404 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "404 Connection rules"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-404 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules (connection rules) that:  (a) are expressed to apply to specified persons; and  (b) relate to any or all of the following:  (i) the connection of specified customer equipment to a telecommunications network or to a facility;  (ii) maintaining a connection referred to in subparagraph (i);  (iii) the connection of specified customer cabling to a telecommunications network or to a facility;  (iv) maintaining a connection referred to in subparagraph (iii). Note 1: A person may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any other way. Note 2: Equipment or cabling may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any other way.  (2) A person specified under paragraph (1)(a) is said to be subject to the connection rules.  (3) The connection rules may make provision for or in relation to a particular matter by empowering the ACMA to make decisions of an administrative character." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACMA may, by legislative instrument, make rules (connection rules) that:  (a) are expressed to apply to specified persons; and  (b) relate to any or all of the following:  (i) the connection of specified customer equipment to a telecommunications network or to a facility;  (ii) maintaining a connection referred to in subparagraph (i);  (iii) the connection of specified customer cabling to a telecommunications network or to a facility;  (iv) maintaining a connection referred to in subparagraph (iii). Note 1: A person may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any other way. Note 2: Equipment or cabling may be specified by name, by inclusion in a specified class or in any other way.  (2) A person specified under paragraph (1)(a) is said to be subject to the connection rules.  (3) The connection rules may make provision for or in relation to a particular matter by empowering the ACMA to make decisions of an administrative character."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ea10a1458f146a5f39938ac1546a8f2195f7a072bce8acc55145dd0b02831c53" ;
    cof:pageNumber "333"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-404-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-404-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-404-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
