concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-437 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "437 Suspension of cabling licence"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-437 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a cabling licence, suspend the cabling licence for a period of not longer than 28 days.  (2) In deciding whether to suspend the cabling licence, the ACMA must have regard to:  (a) any matter to which the ACMA was required, under section 427, to have regard in deciding whether to grant a cabling licence; and  (b) whether or not the holder of the cabling licence has been convicted of an offence against this Division.  (3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which the ACMA may have regard.  (4) During the period of suspension, section 420 has effect as if the licence did not exist." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the holder of a cabling licence, suspend the cabling licence for a period of not longer than 28 days.  (2) In deciding whether to suspend the cabling licence, the ACMA must have regard to:  (a) any matter to which the ACMA was required, under section 427, to have regard in deciding whether to grant a cabling licence; and  (b) whether or not the holder of the cabling licence has been convicted of an offence against this Division.  (3) Subsection (2) does not, by implication, limit the matters to which the ACMA may have regard.  (4) During the period of suspension, section 420 has effect as if the licence did not exist."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1ab39035877bc83956641ad79b3df59e0f2fe7e7a03a6f590e4876423c0f4655" ;
    cof:pageNumber "357"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-437-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-437-ss-2 ;
