concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-442 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "442 Register of cabling licences"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-442 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA is to maintain a Register in which it includes:  (a) all cabling licences currently in force; and  (b) all conditions of such licences.  (2) The Register may be maintained by electronic means.  (3) A person may, on payment of the charge (if any) fixed by a determination under section 60 of the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005:  (a) inspect the Register; and  (b) make a copy of, or take extracts from, the Register.  (4) For the purposes of this section, if the Register is maintained by electronic means, a person is taken to have made a copy of, or taken an extract from, the Register if the ACMA gives the person a printout of, or of the relevant parts of, the Register.  (5) If a person requests that a copy be provided in an electronic form, the ACMA may provide the relevant information:  (a) on a data processing device; or  (b) by way of electronic transmission.   Technical regulation  Part 21 Remedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division  Section 443  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACMA is to maintain a Register in which it includes:  (a) all cabling licences currently in force; and  (b) all conditions of such licences.  (2) The Register may be maintained by electronic means.  (3) A person may, on payment of the charge (if any) fixed by a determination under section 60 of the Australian Communications and Media Authority Act 2005:  (a) inspect the Register; and  (b) make a copy of, or take extracts from, the Register.  (4) For the purposes of this section, if the Register is maintained by electronic means, a person is taken to have made a copy of, or taken an extract from, the Register if the ACMA gives the person a printout of, or of the relevant parts of, the Register.  (5) If a person requests that a copy be provided in an electronic form, the ACMA may provide the relevant information:  (a) on a data processing device; or  (b) by way of electronic transmission.   Technical regulation  Part 21 Remedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division  Section 443  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d2642c95018a3777bec100e12955cfdc645c6338223df5b96ca68332092ade40" ;
    cof:pageNumber "360"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-442-ss-1 ;
