concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-444 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "444 Remedy for contravention of labelling requirements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-444 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person (the first person) contravenes section 413, 414 or 415 in relation to particular customer equipment or particular customer cabling; and   Technical regulation  Part 21 Remedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division  Section 445  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) a person (who may be the first person) connects the equipment or cabling to a telecommunications network or to a facility; and  (c) as a result of:  (i) the connection of the equipment or cabling to the network or facility; or  (ii) the equipment or cabling being used while it was so connected;  either:  (iii) damage is caused to the network or the facility; or  (iv) the manager of the network or facility suffers a loss; the manager of the network or facility may apply to the Federal Court for the recovery from the first person of the amount of the loss or damage.  (2) An application under this section must be made within 3 years after the damage was caused or the loss was suffered, as the case requires." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a person (the first person) contravenes section 413, 414 or 415 in relation to particular customer equipment or particular customer cabling; and   Technical regulation  Part 21 Remedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division  Section 445  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) a person (who may be the first person) connects the equipment or cabling to a telecommunications network or to a facility; and  (c) as a result of:  (i) the connection of the equipment or cabling to the network or facility; or  (ii) the equipment or cabling being used while it was so connected;  either:  (iii) damage is caused to the network or the facility; or  (iv) the manager of the network or facility suffers a loss; the manager of the network or facility may apply to the Federal Court for the recovery from the first person of the amount of the loss or damage.  (2) An application under this section must be made within 3 years after the damage was caused or the loss was suffered, as the case requires."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "379ef88d037012728a7dea193b94c6e8ce50f1697759ed23bab9d8de06af9949" ;
    cof:pageNumber "362"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-444-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-444-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
