doc:sec-444-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "444(1) Remedy for contravention of labelling requirements" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If:  (a) a person (the first person) contravenes section 413, 414 or 415 in relation to particular customer equipment or particular customer cabling; and   Technical regulation  Part 21 Remedies for unauthorised connections to telecommunications networks etc.  Division  Section 445  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) a person (who may be the first person) connects the equipment or cabling to a telecommunications network or to a facility; and  (c) as a result of:  (i) the connection of the equipment or cabling to the network or facility; or  (ii) the equipment or cabling being used while it was so connected;  either:  (iii) damage is caused to the network or the facility; or  (iv) the manager of the network or facility suffers a loss; the manager of the network or facility may apply to the Federal Court for the recovery from the first person of the amount of the loss or damage." ;
    cof:pageNumber "362"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-444-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "444(2) Remedy for contravention of labelling requirements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-444-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) An application under this section must be made within 3 years after the damage was caused or the loss was suffered, as the case requires." ;
    skos:definition "(2) An application under this section must be made within 3 years after the damage was caused or the loss was suffered, as the case requires."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9227dda571102492e4c5f52e45bc06f12c8e9fb7a879710b94cd75fadd82df0a" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-444 ;
