    skos:definition "(1) If:  (a) a person (the first person):  (i) connects customer equipment, or customer cabling, to a telecommunications network or to a facility; or  (ii) has under his or her control customer equipment, or customer cabling, connected to a telecommunications network or to a facility; and  (b) the manager of the network or facility has an honest belief that the equipment or cabling is, or is likely to be, a threat to the integrity of a telecommunications network or a facility; the manager of the network or facility may:  (c) disconnect the equipment or cabling; and  (d) if it is necessary to disconnect other customer equipment or other customer cabling for the purposes of achieving the disconnection referred to in paragraph (c)—disconnect that other equipment or cabling."@en ;
