concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454d a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "454D Revocation of determination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-454d ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, revoke the determination of a person as the numbering scheme manager if:  (a) the Minister is not satisfied the person is managing the numbering scheme in accordance with the numbering scheme principles; or  (b) the Minister is satisfied it is in the best interests of one or more of the following:  (i) the telecommunications industry;  (ii) users of carriage services;  (iii) the general community; or  (c) the Minister is satisfied it is in the best interests of national security.  (2) Before the Minister revokes the determination of a person as the numbering scheme manager, the Minister must consult the person, the ACMA and the ACCC." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, revoke the determination of a person as the numbering scheme manager if:  (a) the Minister is not satisfied the person is managing the numbering scheme in accordance with the numbering scheme principles; or  (b) the Minister is satisfied it is in the best interests of one or more of the following:  (i) the telecommunications industry;  (ii) users of carriage services;  (iii) the general community; or  (c) the Minister is satisfied it is in the best interests of national security.  (2) Before the Minister revokes the determination of a person as the numbering scheme manager, the Minister must consult the person, the ACMA and the ACCC."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a74f7064d71b3cd9362f37d783c9df398c34ff9fd34ac0930b240c6d25cf68c7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "377"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454d-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-454d-ss-2 ;
