concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484j-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "484J(4) Automation of administrative action"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-484j-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The ACMA may make a decision in substitution for a decision the ACMA is treated as having taken under subsection (3) if:  (a) in any case—the ACMA is satisfied that the decision taken by the operation of the computer program is not correct; or  (b) if the decision taken by the operation of the computer program is a decision under subsection 484G(4) to accept one or more sender identifications—the ACMA is satisfied that one or more of those sender identifications are spoofing sender identifications." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The ACMA may make a decision in substitution for a decision the ACMA is treated as having taken under subsection (3) if:  (a) in any case—the ACMA is satisfied that the decision taken by the operation of the computer program is not correct; or  (b) if the decision taken by the operation of the computer program is a decision under subsection 484G(4) to accept one or more sender identifications—the ACMA is satisfied that one or more of those sender identifications are spoofing sender identifications."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2cc8d52f07a40736a3af1ad4906a2918e978931c28bd9bc16c172ebd3b97464a" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-484j ;
    cof:pageNumber "414"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "ACMA may make a decision in substitution for an incorrect computer program decision." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
