concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-492-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "492(3) Hearing to be in public except in exceptional cases"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-492-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) However, the hearing, or a part of the hearing, may be conducted in private if the ACMA is satisfied that:  (a) evidence that may be given, or a matter that may arise, during the hearing or a part of the hearing is of a confidential nature; or  (b) hearing a matter, or part of a matter, in public would not be conducive to the due administration of this Act." ;
    skos:definition "(3) However, the hearing, or a part of the hearing, may be conducted in private if the ACMA is satisfied that:  (a) evidence that may be given, or a matter that may arise, during the hearing or a part of the hearing is of a confidential nature; or  (b) hearing a matter, or part of a matter, in public would not be conducive to the due administration of this Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fe891e488466cf53865a6b531b250ff23ce2e553e21277fdbaae67ea0adb827a" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-492 ;
    cof:pageNumber "423"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Private hearing allowed under exceptional cases" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
