concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-493 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "493 Confidential material not to be published"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-493 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies to a hearing conducted under this Division.  (2) If:  (a) the hearing, or a part of the hearing, takes place in public; and  (b) the ACMA is of the opinion that:  (i) evidence or other material presented to the hearing; or  (ii) material in a written submission lodged with the ACMA;  is of a confidential nature; the ACMA may order that:  (c) the evidence or material not be published; or  (d) its disclosure be restricted.  (3) A person must not fail to comply with an order under subsection (2).  (4) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the ACMA has made an order under subsection (2); and  (b) the person engages in conduct; and  (c) the person’s conduct contravenes the order. Penalty: 50 penalty units.  (5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not apply if the person has a reasonable excuse. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (5) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).  (6) In this section: engage in conduct means:  (a) do an act; or   Public inquiries  Part 25 Inquiries by the ACMA  Division 2  Section 494  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) omit to perform an act." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies to a hearing conducted under this Division.  (2) If:  (a) the hearing, or a part of the hearing, takes place in public; and  (b) the ACMA is of the opinion that:  (i) evidence or other material presented to the hearing; or  (ii) material in a written submission lodged with the ACMA;  is of a confidential nature; the ACMA may order that:  (c) the evidence or material not be published; or  (d) its disclosure be restricted.  (3) A person must not fail to comply with an order under subsection (2).  (4) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the ACMA has made an order under subsection (2); and  (b) the person engages in conduct; and  (c) the person’s conduct contravenes the order. Penalty: 50 penalty units.  (5) Subsections (3) and (4) do not apply if the person has a reasonable excuse. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (5) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).  (6) In this section: engage in conduct means:  (a) do an act; or   Public inquiries  Part 25 Inquiries by the ACMA  Division 2  Section 494  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) omit to perform an act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "55db3750886cbfadc7637ecfae89e4592aac3ec087d521d21ad0fb450b19befe" ;
    cof:pageNumber "424"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-493-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-493-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-493-ss-3 ;
