concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-499 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "499 Discussion paper"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-499 ;
    values:originalText "(1) After deciding to hold a public inquiry about a matter, the ACCC may cause to be prepared a discussion paper that:  (a) identifies the issues that, in the ACCC’s opinion, are relevant to that matter; and  (b) sets out such background material about, and discussion of, those issues as the ACCC thinks appropriate.  (2) The ACCC must make copies of the discussion paper available at each of the ACCC offices. The ACCC may charge a reasonable price for supplying copies of the discussion paper in accordance with this subsection.  (3) The ACCC may otherwise publish the discussion paper, including in electronic form. The ACCC may charge a fee for supplying a publication under this subsection." ;
    skos:definition "(1) After deciding to hold a public inquiry about a matter, the ACCC may cause to be prepared a discussion paper that:  (a) identifies the issues that, in the ACCC’s opinion, are relevant to that matter; and  (b) sets out such background material about, and discussion of, those issues as the ACCC thinks appropriate.  (2) The ACCC must make copies of the discussion paper available at each of the ACCC offices. The ACCC may charge a reasonable price for supplying copies of the discussion paper in accordance with this subsection.  (3) The ACCC may otherwise publish the discussion paper, including in electronic form. The ACCC may charge a fee for supplying a publication under this subsection."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b0b85418a3640c59460df8ded5115629c2ce32b25a24f5d9da258e751fde4733" ;
    cof:pageNumber "428"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-499-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-499-ss-2 ;
