concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-500 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "500 Written submissions and protection from civil actions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-500 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACCC must provide a reasonable opportunity for any member of the public to make a written submission to the ACCC about the matter to which a public inquiry relates.   Public inquiries  Part 25 Inquiries by the ACCC  Division 3  Section 501  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the ACCC is taken not to have provided a reasonable opportunity to make submissions unless there was a period of at least 28 days during which the submissions could be made.  (3) Civil proceedings do not lie against a person in respect of loss, damage or injury of any kind suffered by another person because of the making in good faith of a statement, or the giving in good faith of a document or information, to the ACCC in connection with a public inquiry under this Division.  (4) The rule in subsection (3) applies whether or not the statement is made, or the document or information is given, in connection with a written submission or a public hearing." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The ACCC must provide a reasonable opportunity for any member of the public to make a written submission to the ACCC about the matter to which a public inquiry relates.   Public inquiries  Part 25 Inquiries by the ACCC  Division 3  Section 501  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the ACCC is taken not to have provided a reasonable opportunity to make submissions unless there was a period of at least 28 days during which the submissions could be made.  (3) Civil proceedings do not lie against a person in respect of loss, damage or injury of any kind suffered by another person because of the making in good faith of a statement, or the giving in good faith of a document or information, to the ACCC in connection with a public inquiry under this Division.  (4) The rule in subsection (3) applies whether or not the statement is made, or the document or information is given, in connection with a written submission or a public hearing."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5582be3da939aba4b51bbbb600b8836dbe813ee303b7ecf625812e78e1514686" ;
    cof:pageNumber "428"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-500-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-500-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-500-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-500-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.428" .
doc:sec-500 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "500 Written submissions and protection from civil actions" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACCC must provide a reasonable opportunity for any member of the public to make a written submission to the ACCC about the matter to which a public inquiry relates.   Public inquiries  Part 25 Inquiries by the ACCC  Division 3  Section 501  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the ACCC is taken not to have provided a reasonable opportunity to make submissions unless there was a period of at least 28 days during which the submissions could be made.  (3) Civil proceedings do not lie against a person in respect of loss, damage or injury of any kind suffered by another person because of the making in good faith of a statement, or the giving in good faith of a document or information, to the ACCC in connection with a public inquiry under this Division.  (4) The rule in subsection (3) applies whether or not the statement is made, or the document or information is given, in connection with a written submission or a public hearing." ;
    cof:pageNumber "428"^^xsd:integer .

