concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-504 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "504 Direction about private hearings"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-504 ;
    values:originalText "(1) This section applies to a hearing conducted under this Division.  (2) If the hearing, or a part of the hearing, takes place in private, the ACCC:  (a) must give directions as to the persons who may be present at the hearing or the part of the hearing; and  (b) may give directions restricting the disclosure of evidence or other material presented at the hearing or the part of the hearing.  (3) A person must not fail to comply with a direction under subsection (2)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) This section applies to a hearing conducted under this Division.  (2) If the hearing, or a part of the hearing, takes place in private, the ACCC:  (a) must give directions as to the persons who may be present at the hearing or the part of the hearing; and  (b) may give directions restricting the disclosure of evidence or other material presented at the hearing or the part of the hearing.  (3) A person must not fail to comply with a direction under subsection (2)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7c0e901c224bbc017fe9a8d0db05ba46a843a165cb2bc548a501190ad771970e" ;
