doc:sec-520 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "520 Simplified outline" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "The following is a simplified outline of this Part: • The ACMA may obtain information from carriers, service providers and other persons if the information is relevant to:  (a) the performance of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications functions; or  (b) the exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications powers. • The ACMA may make record-keeping rules that apply to carriers and carriage service providers.   The ACMA’s information-gathering powers  Part 27 Information-gathering powers  Division 2  Section 521  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "448"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-521 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "521 The ACMA may obtain information and documents from"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-521 ;
    values:originalText "carriers and service providers  (1) This section applies to a carrier or a service provider if the ACMA has reason to believe that the carrier or provider:  (a) has information or a document that is relevant to:  (i) the performance of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications functions; or  (ii) the exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications powers; or  (b) is capable of giving evidence which the ACMA has reason to believe is relevant to:  (i) the performance of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications functions; or  (ii) the exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications powers.  (2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the carrier or provider, require the carrier or provider:  (a) to give to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner and form specified in the notice, any such information; or  (b) to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the notice, any such documents; or  (c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the notice, those copies; or  (d) if the carrier or provider is an individual—to appear before the ACMA at a time and place specified in the notice to give any such evidence, either orally or in writing, and produce any such documents; or  (e) if the carrier or provider is a body corporate or a public body—to cause a competent officer of the body to appear" ;
    skos:definition "carriers and service providers  (1) This section applies to a carrier or a service provider if the ACMA has reason to believe that the carrier or provider:  (a) has information or a document that is relevant to:  (i) the performance of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications functions; or  (ii) the exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications powers; or  (b) is capable of giving evidence which the ACMA has reason to believe is relevant to:  (i) the performance of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications functions; or  (ii) the exercise of any of the ACMA’s telecommunications powers.  (2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the carrier or provider, require the carrier or provider:  (a) to give to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner and form specified in the notice, any such information; or  (b) to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the notice, any such documents; or  (c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the notice, those copies; or  (d) if the carrier or provider is an individual—to appear before the ACMA at a time and place specified in the notice to give any such evidence, either orally or in writing, and produce any such documents; or  (e) if the carrier or provider is a body corporate or a public body—to cause a competent officer of the body to appear"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "133e75b53b872f7eea24c859140e660afefb0efad2407f109e479dbab863ddf6" ;
    cof:pageNumber "449"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-521-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-521-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
