    skos:definition "(2) The ACMA may, by written notice given to the carrier or provider, require the carrier or provider:  (a) to give to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner and form specified in the notice, any such information; or  (b) to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the notice, any such documents; or  (c) to make copies of any such documents and to produce to the ACMA, within the period and in the manner specified in the notice, those copies; or  (d) if the carrier or provider is an individual—to appear before the ACMA at a time and place specified in the notice to give any such evidence, either orally or in writing, and produce any such documents; or  (e) if the carrier or provider is a body corporate or a public body—to cause a competent officer of the body to appear"@en ;
