concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-551 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "551 Court may order forfeiture"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-551 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a court convicts a person of an offence against this Act, the court may order the forfeiture to the Commonwealth of anything used or otherwise involved in the commission of the offence.  (2) A reference in this section to an offence against this Act includes a reference to an offence created by section 6 of the Crimes Act 1914 or Part 2.4 of the Criminal Code that relates to this Act.  (3) In this section: this Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a court convicts a person of an offence against this Act, the court may order the forfeiture to the Commonwealth of anything used or otherwise involved in the commission of the offence.  (2) A reference in this section to an offence against this Act includes a reference to an offence created by section 6 of the Crimes Act 1914 or Part 2.4 of the Criminal Code that relates to this Act.  (3) In this section: this Act includes the Telecommunications (Consumer Protection and Service Standards) Act 1999 and regulations under that Act."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a14af26cab2dd7d80516526465515a33a3b40d61b1e556097394b03d19714fb1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "484"^^xsd:integer ;
