    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-556-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "556(3) Deadlines for reaching certain decisions" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The ACMA is taken, for the purposes of this Part, to have made a decision to refuse the application if it has not informed the applicant of its decision before the end of the relevant period of 90 days.   Review of decisions  Part 29  Section 557  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "486"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-557 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "557 Statements to accompany notification of decisions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-557 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the ACMA makes a decision of a kind referred to in section 555 and gives written notice of the decision to a person whose interests it affects, the notice must include:  (a) a statement to the effect that a person affected by the decision may, if he or she is dissatisfied with the decision, seek a reconsideration of the decision by the ACMA under subsection 558(1); and  (b) a statement to the effect that, if a person who has applied for a reconsideration is dissatisfied with the ACMA’s decision on the reconsideration:  (i) subject to the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024, application may be made to the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of the decision on that reconsideration; and  (ii) the person may request a statement of reasons under section 268 of that Act in relation to the decision on that reconsideration.  (2) Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of a decision." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If the ACMA makes a decision of a kind referred to in section 555 and gives written notice of the decision to a person whose interests it affects, the notice must include:  (a) a statement to the effect that a person affected by the decision may, if he or she is dissatisfied with the decision, seek a reconsideration of the decision by the ACMA under subsection 558(1); and  (b) a statement to the effect that, if a person who has applied for a reconsideration is dissatisfied with the ACMA’s decision on the reconsideration:  (i) subject to the Administrative Review Tribunal Act 2024, application may be made to the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of the decision on that reconsideration; and  (ii) the person may request a statement of reasons under section 268 of that Act in relation to the decision on that reconsideration.  (2) Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of a decision."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "8cc93cca7acd9134964dabcad65afac267c1986c714b5c1711ca73aff247f423" ;
    cof:pageNumber "487"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-557-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-557-ss-2 ;
