doc:sec-577ba-ss-2a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "577BA(2A) Authorised conduct—subsection 51(1) of the Competition and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2A) The giving by a designated Telstra successor company of:  (a) a variation of an undertaking in force under section 577A; or  (b) a variation of a final migration plan; is authorised for the purposes of subsection 51(1) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010." ;
    cof:pageNumber "534"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577ba-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "577BA(3) Authorised conduct—subsection 51(1) of the Competition and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-577ba-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) If:  (a) Telstra enters into a contract, arrangement or understanding with an NBN corporation; and  (b) when the contract, arrangement or understanding is entered into, no undertaking is in force under section 577A; and  (c) the operative provisions of the contract, arrangement or understanding are subject to a condition precedent, namely, the coming into force of an undertaking under section 577A; then:  (d) the entering into of the contract, arrangement or understanding by Telstra is authorised for the purposes of subsection 51(1) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; and  (e) the entering into of the contract, arrangement or understanding by the NBN corporation is authorised for the purposes of subsection 51(1) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; and  (f) if:  (i) the undertaking under section 577A comes into force; and  (ii) if the contract, arrangement or understanding was in writing—before the undertaking was accepted by the ACCC, Telstra or the NBN corporation gave the ACCC a copy of the contract, arrangement or understanding; and  (iii) if the contract, arrangement or understanding was not in writing—before the undertaking was accepted by the ACCC, the contract, arrangement or understanding was reduced to writing and Telstra or the NBN corporation" ;
    skos:definition "(3) If:  (a) Telstra enters into a contract, arrangement or understanding with an NBN corporation; and  (b) when the contract, arrangement or understanding is entered into, no undertaking is in force under section 577A; and  (c) the operative provisions of the contract, arrangement or understanding are subject to a condition precedent, namely, the coming into force of an undertaking under section 577A; then:  (d) the entering into of the contract, arrangement or understanding by Telstra is authorised for the purposes of subsection 51(1) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; and  (e) the entering into of the contract, arrangement or understanding by the NBN corporation is authorised for the purposes of subsection 51(1) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; and  (f) if:  (i) the undertaking under section 577A comes into force; and  (ii) if the contract, arrangement or understanding was in writing—before the undertaking was accepted by the ACCC, Telstra or the NBN corporation gave the ACCC a copy of the contract, arrangement or understanding; and  (iii) if the contract, arrangement or understanding was not in writing—before the undertaking was accepted by the ACCC, the contract, arrangement or understanding was reduced to writing and Telstra or the NBN corporation"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "16325ec2b03409abda4a1402f0bb9be5efec57b9393ad70a99458fda4f0262c5" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577ba ;
    cof:pageNumber "534"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorisation for entering into contracts with NBN corporations under section 51(1) of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-act-1997.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-act-1997.pdf, p.534" ;
