doc:sec-577c-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "577C(1) Acceptance of undertaking about hybrid fibre-coaxial" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACCC may accept a written undertaking given by Telstra that:  (a) at all times after the end of the period specified in the undertaking, Telstra will not be in a position to exercise control of a hybrid fibre-coaxial network in Australia; and  (b) Telstra will, in connection with paragraph (a), take specified action and/or refrain from taking specified action. Note: For when Telstra is in a position to exercise control of a network, see section 577Q." ;
    cof:pageNumber "561"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577c-ss-1a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "577C(1A) Acceptance of undertaking about hybrid fibre-coaxial"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-577c-ss-1a ;
    values:originalText "(1A) In deciding whether to accept an undertaking under subsection (1), the ACCC must have regard to:  (a) the matters (if any) set out in an instrument in force under subsection (1B); and  (b) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant." ;
    skos:definition "(1A) In deciding whether to accept an undertaking under subsection (1), the ACCC must have regard to:  (a) the matters (if any) set out in an instrument in force under subsection (1B); and  (b) such other matters (if any) as the ACCC considers relevant."@en ;
