doc:sec-577j-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "577J(1) Limits on allocation of certain spectrum licences to Telstra" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If the excluded spectrum regime applies to Telstra, the ACMA must not allocate a spectrum licence to Telstra if the licence relates to a designated part of the spectrum. Note: For excluded spectrum regime, see section 577GA.   Voluntary undertakings originally given by Telstra  Part 33 Limits on allocation of spectrum licences etc.  Division 6  Section 577J  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
