concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-577j-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "577J(2) Limits on allocation of certain spectrum licences to Telstra"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-577j-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) However, the rule in subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) both:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577A; and  (ii) the undertaking is covered by subsection (2A); and  (b) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577C; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection (3); and  (c) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577E; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection (5). Note 1: Section 577A deals with undertakings about structural separation. Note 2: Section 577C deals with undertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks. Note 3: Section 577E deals with undertakings about subscription television broadcasting licences." ;
    skos:definition "(2) However, the rule in subsection (1) does not apply if:  (a) both:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577A; and  (ii) the undertaking is covered by subsection (2A); and  (b) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577C; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection (3); and  (c) either:  (i) an undertaking given by Telstra is in force under section 577E; or  (ii) a declaration is in force under subsection (5). Note 1: Section 577A deals with undertakings about structural separation. Note 2: Section 577C deals with undertakings about hybrid fibre-coaxial networks. Note 3: Section 577E deals with undertakings about subscription television broadcasting licences."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d5dbdeff4a3eb3a74d9f21c320f55a74517e1f64c21a53c9e445afd1b80aa06c" ;
