doc:sec-581 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "581 Power to give directions to carriers and service providers" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The ACMA may give written directions to:  (a) a carrier; or  (b) a service provider; in connection with performing any of the ACMA’s telecommunications functions or exercising any of the ACMA’s telecommunications powers.  (2) This section is not limited by any other provision of a law that:  (a) confers a function or power on the ACMA; or  (b) prescribes the mode in which the ACMA is to perform a function or exercise a power; or  (c) prescribes conditions or restrictions which must be observed in relation to the performance by the ACMA of a function or the exercise by the ACMA of a power.  (2A) The eSafety Commissioner may give written directions to:  (a) a carrier; or  (b) a service provider; in connection with performing any of the Commissioner’s functions or exercising any of the Commissioner’s powers.  (2B) This section is not limited by any other provision of a law that:  (a) confers a function or power on the eSafety Commissioner; or  (b) prescribes the mode in which the eSafety Commissioner is to perform a function or exercise a power; or  (c) prescribes conditions or restrictions which must be observed in relation to the performance by the eSafety Commissioner of a function or the exercise by the eSafety Commissioner of a power.   Special provisions relating to conventions and directions  Part 34  Section 581  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (4) A person must comply with a direction given to the person under subsection (1).  (4A) A person must comply with a direction given to the person under subsection (2A)." ;
    cof:pageNumber "592"^^xsd:integer .

