concept:telecommunications-act-1997-sec-581h a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "581H Declarations—criteria"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-581h ;
    values:originalText "(1) In deciding whether to specify a company (the relevant company) in a declaration under subsection 581F(3), (4) or (5) or 581G(3), (4) or (5), the Minister must have regard to the following matters:   Telstra successor companies and designated Telstra successor companies  Part 34A Telstra successor company and designated Telstra successor company  Division 2  Section 581J  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) the object set out in section 581B;  (b) the compliance burden (if any) that would result for the relevant company if the declaration were made;  (c) whether a Telstra successor company or a designated Telstra successor company has transferred the whole or a part of a telecommunications business to the relevant company;  (d) whether a Telstra successor company or a designated Telstra successor company has transferred a telecommunications asset to the relevant company;  (e) such other matters (if any) as the Minister considers relevant.  (2) The Minister must not specify a company in a declaration under subsection 581F(3), (4) or (5) or 581G(3), (4) or (5) unless the company:  (a) is a constitutional corporation; or  (b) carries on a telecommunications business covered by paragraph 581L(1)(a), (b) or (c)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) In deciding whether to specify a company (the relevant company) in a declaration under subsection 581F(3), (4) or (5) or 581G(3), (4) or (5), the Minister must have regard to the following matters:   Telstra successor companies and designated Telstra successor companies  Part 34A Telstra successor company and designated Telstra successor company  Division 2  Section 581J  Telecommunications Act 1997  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) the object set out in section 581B;  (b) the compliance burden (if any) that would result for the relevant company if the declaration were made;  (c) whether a Telstra successor company or a designated Telstra successor company has transferred the whole or a part of a telecommunications business to the relevant company;  (d) whether a Telstra successor company or a designated Telstra successor company has transferred a telecommunications asset to the relevant company;  (e) such other matters (if any) as the Minister considers relevant.  (2) The Minister must not specify a company in a declaration under subsection 581F(3), (4) or (5) or 581G(3), (4) or (5) unless the company:  (a) is a constitutional corporation; or  (b) carries on a telecommunications business covered by paragraph 581L(1)(a), (b) or (c)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "c5795e4f708653e76a487845a479284af5fe27f8fb3b2301d8b7e466d30ce87f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "600"^^xsd:integer ;
